IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`
IMPORT `sfad-nocons-small-private`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, part sfad: Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (4), s 273, "Offer made under certain circumstances" (lines 43382-44137 of SFA2001.txt).
-- Imports prelude, daydate, sfa-core and sfa-periods (every period is counted by sfa-periods, never here).
--
-- How to read a function in this module.
--   Section 273(1) says that Subdivisions (2) and (3) (other than section 257) "do not apply to an offer ... if" the offer comes within any one of
--   paragraphs (a) to (k). Each paragraph is its own function. A paragraph's function answers JUST TRUE when the facts put the offer in the paragraph,
--   JUST FALSE when they do not (the paragraph says what the offer "is"; a condition of the "if" list, read under the rule of 2026-10-29 (a)), and
--   NOTHING where a fact the paragraph turns on is not known. The function for subsection (1) takes every paragraph's answer in a list.
--   What the Authority may prescribe (excluded shares, debentures, units, contracts, organised markets, disclosure requirements) is an INPUT.
--   "-- FORK" lines are collected into the fork register of NOTES.md.


§ `s 273(9) and (10): the unlisted corporation, and the corporation that is not a company`

-- src:44124 | (9) In subsection (1)(b) and (c), “unlisted corporation” means a
-- src:44125 | corporation —
-- src:44127 | (a) that is not a company; and
-- src:44129 | (b) the shares or debentures, or units of shares or debentures,
-- src:44130 | of which are not listed for quotation on any approved
-- src:44131 | exchange.
@ref s 273(9) (src:44124-44131)
GIVEN
    `the corporation is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a company?
    `the shares or debentures, or units of shares or debentures, of the corporation are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares or debentures, or units of shares or debentures, of the corporation listed for quotation on any approved exchange?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(9) the corporation is an unlisted corporation` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the corporation is a company`) AND (NOT `the shares or debentures, or units of shares or debentures, of the corporation are listed for quotation on an approved exchange`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“unlisted corporation” means a corporation — (a) that is not a company; and (b) the shares or debentures, or units of shares or debentures, of which are not listed for quotation on any approved exchange"

-- src:44135 | (10) In subsection (1)(ca) and (cb), “corporation” means a
-- src:44136 | corporation that is not a company.
@ref s 273(10) (src:44135-44136)
GIVEN
    `the corporation is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(10) the corporation is a corporation for paragraphs (ca) and (cb)` MEANS
    IF `the corporation is a company`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“corporation” means a corporation that is not a company"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `s 273(1)(a) to (cc): take-overs, compromises and underwriting`

-- src:43388 | (a) it is made in connection with a take‑over offer which is in
-- src:43389 | compliance with the Take‑over Code;
@ref s 273(1)(a) (src:43388-43389)
GIVEN
    `the offer is made in connection with a take-over offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made in connection with a take-over offer?
    `the take-over offer is in compliance with the Take-over Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the take-over offer in compliance with the Take-over Code?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(a) the offer is made in connection with a take-over offer in compliance with the Take-over Code` MEANS
    IF `the offer is made in connection with a take-over offer` AND `the take-over offer is in compliance with the Take-over Code`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is made in connection with a take-over offer which is in compliance with the Take-over Code"

-- src:43391 | (b) it is made in connection with an offer for the acquisition by
-- src:43392 | or on behalf of a person of some or all of the shares in an
-- src:43393 | unlisted corporation or some or all of the shares of a
-- src:43394 | particular class in an unlisted corporation —
-- src:43396 | (i) to all members of the corporation or all members of
-- src:43397 | the corporation holding shares of that class; or
-- src:43402 | (ii) where the person already holds shares in the
-- src:43403 | corporation, to all other members of the
-- src:43404 | corporation or all other members of the corporation
-- src:43405 | holding shares of that class,
-- src:43407 | (b) where such offer is in compliance with the laws, codes and
-- src:43408 | other requirements (whether or not having the force of law)
-- src:43409 | relating to take‑overs of the country in which the
-- src:43410 | corporation was incorporated;
@ref s 273(1)(b) (src:43391-43410)
GIVEN
    `the offer is made in connection with an offer for the acquisition by or on behalf of a person of some or all of the shares, or of some or all of the shares of a particular class, in an unlisted corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made in connection with an offer for the acquisition, by or on behalf of a person, of some or all of the shares in an unlisted corporation, or some or all of the shares of a particular class in it?
    `the acquisition offer is made to all members of the corporation, or all members holding shares of that class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the acquisition offer made to all members of the corporation, or all the members holding shares of that class?
    `the person already holds shares in the corporation and the acquisition offer is made to all other members, or all other members holding shares of that class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where the person already holds shares in the corporation, is the acquisition offer made to all other members of the corporation, or all other members holding shares of that class?
    `the acquisition offer is in compliance with the laws, codes and other requirements relating to take-overs of the country in which the corporation was incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the acquisition offer in compliance with the laws, codes and other requirements (whether or not having the force of law) relating to take-overs of the country in which the corporation was incorporated?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(b) the offer is made in connection with an acquisition offer for the shares of an unlisted corporation` MEANS
    IF `the offer is made in connection with an offer for the acquisition by or on behalf of a person of some or all of the shares, or of some or all of the shares of a particular class, in an unlisted corporation` AND (`the acquisition offer is made to all members of the corporation, or all members holding shares of that class` OR `the person already holds shares in the corporation and the acquisition offer is made to all other members, or all other members holding shares of that class`) AND `the acquisition offer is in compliance with the laws, codes and other requirements relating to take-overs of the country in which the corporation was incorporated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is made in connection with an offer for the acquisition by or on behalf of a person of some or all of the shares in an unlisted corporation"
    -- The paragraph's own "unlisted corporation" is the term of subsection (9): the caller asks `s 273(9) the corporation is an unlisted corporation` and states the answer in the first input.

-- src:43412 | (c) it is made in connection with a proposed compromise or
-- src:43413 | arrangement between —
-- src:43415 | (i) an unlisted corporation and its creditors or a class of
-- src:43416 | them; or
-- src:43418 | (ii) an unlisted corporation and its members or a class of
-- src:43419 | them,
-- src:43421 | (c) and such proposed compromise or arrangement and the
