    `the offer is made in connection with a proposed compromise or arrangement between an unlisted corporation and its creditors or a class of them, or its members or a class of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made in connection with a proposed compromise or arrangement between an unlisted corporation and its creditors (or a class of them), or between an unlisted corporation and its members (or a class of them)?
    `the proposed compromise or arrangement and the execution of it is in compliance with the laws, codes and other requirements of the country in which the corporation was incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proposed compromise or arrangement, and the execution of it, in compliance with the laws, codes and other requirements (whether or not having the force of law) relating to take-overs, compromises and arrangements of the country in which the corporation was incorporated?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(c) the offer is made in connection with a compromise or arrangement of an unlisted corporation` MEANS
    IF `the offer is made in connection with a proposed compromise or arrangement between an unlisted corporation and its creditors or a class of them, or its members or a class of them` AND `the proposed compromise or arrangement and the execution of it is in compliance with the laws, codes and other requirements of the country in which the corporation was incorporated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is made in connection with a proposed compromise or arrangement between"

-- src:43427 | (ca) it is made in connection with an offer for the acquisition by
-- src:43428 | or on behalf of a person of some or all of the shares in a
-- src:43429 | corporation or some or all of the shares of a particular class
-- src:43430 | in a corporation —
