§ `s 273(1AA), (1AB), (1AC): listing through SDRs`

-- src:43865 | (1AA) For the purposes of subsection (1)(cd) and (cda), securities
-- src:43866 | of an entity are treated as being listed for quotation on an approved
-- src:43867 | exchange if SDRs with securities of the entity as the underlying
-- src:43868 | securities are listed for quotation on the approved exchange.
@ref s 273(1AA) (src:43865-43868)
GIVEN
    `the securities of the entity are listed for quotation on the approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities of the entity listed for quotation on the approved exchange?
    `SDRs with securities of the entity as the underlying securities are listed for quotation on the approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are SDRs with securities of the entity as the underlying securities listed for quotation on the approved exchange?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1AA) the securities of the entity are treated as listed for quotation on the approved exchange` MEANS
    IF `the securities of the entity are listed for quotation on the approved exchange` OR `SDRs with securities of the entity as the underlying securities are listed for quotation on the approved exchange`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "securities of an entity are treated as being listed for quotation on an approved exchange if SDRs with securities of the entity as the underlying securities are listed for quotation on the approved exchange"
    -- FORK s273-1AA | s 273(1)(cd) and (cda) | `s 273(1AA) the securities of the entity are treated as listed for quotation on the approved exchange` | took NOTHING where neither the securities nor the SDRs are listed (a deeming that extends "listed"; it does not say the securities are not listed otherwise) | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {IN-SHORT} ("includes" and an extension answer NOTHING); the listing question itself is asked as the first input, so a caller who says the securities are not listed and the SDRs are not either gets NOTHING here and JUST FALSE from the paragraph

-- src:43872 | (1AB) For the purposes of subsection (1)(ce) and (cg)(iii), shares of
-- src:43873 | an entity are treated as being listed for quotation on an approved
-- src:43874 | exchange if SDRs with shares of the entity as the underlying
-- src:43875 | securities are listed for quotation on the approved exchange.
@ref s 273(1AB) (src:43872-43875)
GIVEN
    `the shares of the entity are listed for quotation on the approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares of the entity listed for quotation on the approved exchange?
    `SDRs with shares of the entity as the underlying securities are listed for quotation on the approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are SDRs with shares of the entity as the underlying securities listed for quotation on the approved exchange?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1AB) the shares of the entity are treated as listed for quotation on the approved exchange` MEANS
    IF `the shares of the entity are listed for quotation on the approved exchange` OR `SDRs with shares of the entity as the underlying securities are listed for quotation on the approved exchange`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shares of an entity are treated as being listed for quotation on an approved exchange if SDRs with shares of the entity as the underlying securities are listed for quotation on the approved exchange"

