GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of SDRs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of sponsored depositary receipts (SDRs)?
    `the securities are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 273(1AA) says` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities of the entity listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs with those securities as the underlying securities as section 273(1AA) says?
    `the entity is not formed or constituted in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity not formed or constituted in Singapore?
    `the listing is a primary listing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the listing on the approved exchange a primary listing?
    `the offer is made to existing members or debenture holders of that entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made to existing members or debenture holders of the entity?
    `the offer is made to existing holders of SDRs with shares or debentures of that entity as the underlying securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made to existing holders of SDRs with shares or debentures of the entity as the underlying securities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(cda) the offer is an offer of SDRs whose underlying securities are of an unlisted entity, or a non-primary listing, made to existing members, debenture holders or SDR holders` MEANS
    IF `the offer is an offer of SDRs` AND ((NOT `the securities are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 273(1AA) says`) OR (`the entity is not formed or constituted in Singapore` AND `the securities are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 273(1AA) says` AND (NOT `the listing is a primary listing`))) AND (`the offer is made to existing members or debenture holders of that entity` OR `the offer is made to existing holders of SDRs with shares or debentures of that entity as the underlying securities`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is an offer of SDRs, where the entity whose securities are the underlying securities of those SDRs"

