    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is an offer of shares or debentures of an entity, or of SDRs with shares or debentures of an entity as the underlying securities, made to"

-- src:43534 | (cf) it is an offer of debentures of an entity made to any existing
-- src:43535 | debenture holder of the entity whose debentures are listed
-- src:43536 | for quotation on an approved exchange;
@ref s 273(1)(cf) (src:43534-43536)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of debentures of an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of debentures of an entity?
    `the offer is made to an existing debenture holder of the entity whose debentures are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made to an existing debenture holder of the entity whose debentures are listed for quotation on an approved exchange?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(cf) the offer of debentures is made to an existing holder of listed debentures` MEANS
    IF `the offer is an offer of debentures of an entity` AND `the offer is made to an existing debenture holder of the entity whose debentures are listed for quotation on an approved exchange`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is an offer of debentures of an entity made to any existing debenture holder of the entity whose debentures are listed for quotation on an approved exchange"

-- src:43538 | (cg) it is an offer of units of shares or debentures of an entity
-- src:43539 | made to —
-- src:43541 | (i) any existing member or debenture holder of that
-- src:43542 | entity; or
-- src:43544 | (ii) any existing holder of an SDR with shares or
-- src:43545 | debentures of that entity as the underlying securities,
-- src:43547 | (cg) (called X in this paragraph), where —
-- src:43549 | (iii) shares of that entity are listed for quotation on an
-- src:43550 | approved exchange; and
-- src:43555 | (iv) such units may only be exercised or converted by X
-- src:43556 | into shares or debentures (as the case may be) of that
-- src:43557 | entity;
@ref s 273(1)(cg) (src:43538-43557)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of units of shares or debentures of an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of units of shares or debentures of an entity?
    `the offer is made to an existing member or debenture holder of that entity, or an existing holder of an SDR with shares or debentures of that entity as the underlying securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made to an existing member or debenture holder of the entity, or to an existing holder of an SDR with shares or debentures of the entity as the underlying securities?
    `the shares of the entity are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 273(1)(ce) and (cg)(iii) say` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares of the entity listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs with shares of the entity as the underlying securities as section 273(1AB) says?
    `the units may only be exercised or converted by the person offered into shares or debentures of that entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the units be exercised or converted only by the person to whom they are offered, into shares or debentures of the entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(cg) the offer of units of shares or debentures is made to existing holders where the shares are listed and the units may only be exercised by them` MEANS
    IF `the offer is an offer of units of shares or debentures of an entity` AND `the offer is made to an existing member or debenture holder of that entity, or an existing holder of an SDR with shares or debentures of that entity as the underlying securities` AND `the shares of the entity are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 273(1)(ce) and (cg)(iii) say` AND `the units may only be exercised or converted by the person offered into shares or debentures of that entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is an offer of units of shares or debentures of an entity made to"

-- src:43561 | (ch) it is an offer of units of debentures of an entity made to any
-- src:43562 | existing debenture holder of the entity whose debentures
-- src:43563 | are listed on an approved exchange, where such units may
-- src:43564 | only be exercised or converted by any existing debenture
-- src:43565 | holder into debentures of the entity;
@ref s 273(1)(ch) (src:43561-43565)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of units of debentures of an entity made to an existing debenture holder of the entity whose debentures are listed on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of units of debentures of an entity made to an existing debenture holder of the entity whose debentures are listed on an approved exchange?
    `the units may only be exercised or converted by any existing debenture holder into debentures of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the units be exercised or converted only by an existing debenture holder, into debentures of the entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(ch) the offer of units of debentures is made to an existing holder of listed debentures and the units may only be exercised by holders` MEANS
    IF `the offer is an offer of units of debentures of an entity made to an existing debenture holder of the entity whose debentures are listed on an approved exchange` AND `the units may only be exercised or converted by any existing debenture holder into debentures of the entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is an offer of units of debentures of an entity made to any existing debenture holder of the entity whose debentures are listed on an approved exchange"

-- src:43567 | (ci) it is an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:43568 | contracts of a corporation made in the circumstances
-- src:43569 | specified under section 178 of the Insolvency,
-- src:43570 | Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018;
@ref s 273(1)(ci) (src:43567-43570)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation made in the circumstances specified under section 178 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation, made in the circumstances specified under section 178 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(ci) the offer is made in the circumstances specified under section 178 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` MEANS
    IF `the offer is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation made in the circumstances specified under section 178 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of a corporation made in the circumstances specified under section 178"


-- src:43572 | (cj) it is an offer of —
-- src:43574 | (i) units in a business trust; or
-- src:43576 | (ii) SDRs with units in a business trust as the underlying
-- src:43577 | securities,
-- src:43579 | (cj) being a business trust whose units are listed for quotation
-- src:43580 | on an approved exchange, where the offer is made to —
-- src:43582 | (iii) any existing unitholder of the business trust;
-- src:43584 | (iv) any existing holder of any debenture of the
-- src:43585 | trustee‑manager of the business trust that is issued
-- src:43586 | by the trustee‑manager of the business trust in its
-- src:43587 | capacity as trustee‑manager of the business trust
-- src:43588 | (called in this paragraph a debenture of the business
-- src:43589 | trust); or
-- src:43591 | (v) any existing holder of an SDR with units in the
-- src:43592 | business trust or debentures of the business trust as
-- src:43593 | the underlying securities;
@ref s 273(1)(cj) (src:43572-43593)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of units in a business trust, or of SDRs with units in a business trust as the underlying securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of units in a business trust, or of SDRs with units in a business trust as the underlying securities?
    `the units of the business trust are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 273(1AC) says` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the units of the business trust listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs with units in the business trust as the underlying securities as section 273(1AC) says?
    `the offer is made to an existing unitholder of the business trust, an existing holder of a debenture of the trustee-manager issued in its capacity as trustee-manager, or an existing holder of an SDR with units in the business trust or debentures of the business trust as the underlying securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made to an existing unitholder of the business trust, to an existing holder of a debenture of the trustee-manager issued by it in its capacity as trustee-manager of the business trust, or to an existing holder of an SDR with units in the business trust or debentures of the business trust as the underlying securities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(cj) the offer of units in a listed business trust is made to existing holders` MEANS
    IF `the offer is an offer of units in a business trust, or of SDRs with units in a business trust as the underlying securities` AND `the units of the business trust are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 273(1AC) says` AND `the offer is made to an existing unitholder of the business trust, an existing holder of a debenture of the trustee-manager issued in its capacity as trustee-manager, or an existing holder of an SDR with units in the business trust or debentures of the business trust as the underlying securities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is an offer of — (i) units in a business trust; or (ii) SDRs with units in a business trust as the underlying securities"

-- src:43597 | (ck) it is an offer of derivatives of units in a business trust,
-- src:43598 | whose units are listed for quotation on an approved
-- src:43599 | exchange, made to —
-- src:43604 | (i) any existing unitholder of the business trust, where
-- src:43605 | such derivatives of units may only be exercised or
-- src:43606 | converted by the existing unitholder into units of the
-- src:43607 | business trust;
-- src:43611 | (ii) any existing holder of any debenture of the
-- src:43612 | trustee‑manager of the business trust that is issued
-- src:43613 | by the trustee‑manager of the business trust in its
-- src:43614 | capacity as trustee‑manager of the business trust
-- src:43615 | (called in this paragraph a debenture of the business
-- src:43616 | trust), where such derivatives of units may only be
-- src:43617 | exercised or converted by the existing holder into
-- src:43618 | units in the business trust; or
-- src:43622 | (iii) any existing holder of an SDR with units in the
-- src:43623 | business trust or debentures of the business trust as
-- src:43624 | the underlying securities, where such derivatives of
-- src:43625 | units may only be exercised or converted by the
-- src:43626 | existing holder into units in the business trust;
@ref s 273(1)(ck) (src:43597-43626)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of derivatives of units in a business trust whose units are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of derivatives of units in a business trust whose units are listed for quotation on an approved exchange?
    `the offer is made to an existing unitholder of the business trust, an existing holder of a debenture of the trustee-manager issued in its capacity as trustee-manager, or an existing holder of an SDR with units in the business trust or debentures of the business trust as the underlying securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made to an existing unitholder of the business trust, to an existing holder of a debenture of the trustee-manager issued by it in its capacity as trustee-manager of the business trust, or to an existing holder of an SDR with units in the business trust or debentures of the business trust as the underlying securities?
    `the derivatives may only be exercised or converted by the person offered into units of the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the derivatives of units be exercised or converted only by the person to whom they are offered, into units in the business trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(ck) the offer of derivatives of units in a listed business trust is made to existing holders who alone may exercise them` MEANS
    IF `the offer is an offer of derivatives of units in a business trust whose units are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` AND `the offer is made to an existing unitholder of the business trust, an existing holder of a debenture of the trustee-manager issued in its capacity as trustee-manager, or an existing holder of an SDR with units in the business trust or debentures of the business trust as the underlying securities` AND `the derivatives may only be exercised or converted by the person offered into units of the business trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is an offer of derivatives of units in a business trust, whose units are listed for quotation on an approved exchange"

-- src:43630 | (cl) it is an offer of units or derivatives of units in a business
-- src:43631 | trust —
-- src:43633 | (i) being a business trust which is registered in
-- src:43634 | Singapore or otherwise, whose units or derivatives
-- src:43635 | of units are not listed for quotation on an approved
-- src:43636 | exchange; or
-- src:43638 | (ii) being a business trust which is not registered in
-- src:43639 | Singapore, whose units or derivatives of units are
-- src:43640 | listed for quotation on an approved exchange and
-- src:43641 | such listing is not a primary listing,
-- src:43643 | (cl) where the offer is made to —
-- src:43645 | (iii) any existing unitholder of the business trust;
-- src:43647 | (iv) any existing holder of any debenture of the
-- src:43648 | trustee‑manager of the business trust that is issued
-- src:43649 | by the trustee‑manager of the business trust in its
-- src:43650 | capacity as trustee‑manager of the business trust
-- src:43655 | (called in this paragraph a debenture of the business
-- src:43656 | trust); or
-- src:43658 | (v) any existing holder of an SDR with units in the
-- src:43659 | business trust or debentures of the business trust as
-- src:43660 | the underlying securities,
-- src:43662 | (cl) (called X in this paragraph), whether or not the offer is
-- src:43663 | renounceable in favour of persons other than X;
@ref s 273(1)(cl) (src:43630-43663)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of units or derivatives of units in a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of units or derivatives of units in a business trust?
    `the units of the business trust are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 273(1AC) says` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the units of the business trust listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs with units in the business trust as the underlying securities as section 273(1AC) says?
    `the business trust is not registered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business trust not registered in Singapore?
    `the listing is a primary listing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the listing on the approved exchange a primary listing?
    `the offer is made to an existing unitholder of the business trust, an existing holder of a debenture of the trustee-manager issued in its capacity as trustee-manager, or an existing holder of an SDR with units in the business trust or debentures of the business trust as the underlying securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made to an existing unitholder of the business trust, to an existing holder of a debenture of the trustee-manager issued by it in its capacity as trustee-manager of the business trust, or to an existing holder of an SDR with units in the business trust or debentures of the business trust as the underlying securities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(cl) the offer of units or derivatives of units is made to existing holders of an unlisted business trust, or a non-primary listing` MEANS
    IF `the offer is an offer of units or derivatives of units in a business trust` AND ((NOT `the units of the business trust are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 273(1AC) says`) OR (`the business trust is not registered in Singapore` AND `the units of the business trust are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 273(1AC) says` AND (NOT `the listing is a primary listing`))) AND `the offer is made to an existing unitholder of the business trust, an existing holder of a debenture of the trustee-manager issued in its capacity as trustee-manager, or an existing holder of an SDR with units in the business trust or debentures of the business trust as the underlying securities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is an offer of units or derivatives of units in a business trust"

-- src:43669 | (cm) it is an offer of SDRs with units in a business trust as the
-- src:43670 | underlying securities, being a business trust —
-- src:43672 | (i) which is registered in Singapore or otherwise, and
-- src:43673 | the units or derivatives of units of which are not
-- src:43674 | listed for quotation on an approved exchange; or
-- src:43676 | (ii) which is not registered in Singapore, and the units or
-- src:43677 | derivatives of units of which are listed for quotation
-- src:43678 | on an approved exchange and such listing is not a
-- src:43679 | primary listing,
-- src:43681 | (cm) where the offer is made to —
-- src:43683 | (iii) any existing unitholder of the business trust;
-- src:43685 | (iv) any existing holder of any debenture of the
-- src:43686 | trustee‑manager of the business trust that is issued
-- src:43687 | by the trustee‑manager of the business trust in its
-- src:43688 | capacity as trustee‑manager of the business trust
-- src:43689 | (called in this paragraph a debenture of the business
-- src:43690 | trust); or
-- src:43692 | (v) any existing holder of an SDR with units in the
-- src:43693 | business trust or debentures of the business trust as
-- src:43694 | the underlying securities,
-- src:43696 | (cm) (called X in this paragraph), whether or not the offer is
-- src:43697 | renounceable in favour of persons other than X;
@ref s 273(1)(cm) (src:43669-43697)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of SDRs with units in a business trust as the underlying securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of SDRs with units in a business trust as the underlying securities?
    `the units of the business trust are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 273(1AC) says` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the units of the business trust listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs with units in the business trust as the underlying securities as section 273(1AC) says?
    `the business trust is not registered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business trust not registered in Singapore?
    `the listing is a primary listing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the listing on the approved exchange a primary listing?
    `the offer is made to an existing unitholder of the business trust, an existing holder of a debenture of the trustee-manager issued in its capacity as trustee-manager, or an existing holder of an SDR with units in the business trust or debentures of the business trust as the underlying securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made to an existing unitholder of the business trust, to an existing holder of a debenture of the trustee-manager issued by it in its capacity as trustee-manager of the business trust, or to an existing holder of an SDR with units in the business trust or debentures of the business trust as the underlying securities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(cm) the offer of SDRs with units in a business trust is made to existing holders of an unlisted business trust, or a non-primary listing` MEANS
    IF `the offer is an offer of SDRs with units in a business trust as the underlying securities` AND ((NOT `the units of the business trust are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 273(1AC) says`) OR (`the business trust is not registered in Singapore` AND `the units of the business trust are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 273(1AC) says` AND (NOT `the listing is a primary listing`))) AND `the offer is made to an existing unitholder of the business trust, an existing holder of a debenture of the trustee-manager issued in its capacity as trustee-manager, or an existing holder of an SDR with units in the business trust or debentures of the business trust as the underlying securities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is an offer of SDRs with units in a business trust as the underlying securities, being a business trust"

§ `s 273(1A), (1AAA) and (1B): borrowed securities, and business trusts`

-- src:43887 | (1A) An offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:43888 | does not come within subsection (1)(d), (da), (e), (ea) or (h) if —
-- src:43890 | (a) the securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:43891 | being offered are borrowed by the issuer from any of the
-- src:43892 | following persons solely for the purpose of facilitating the
-- src:43893 | offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:43894 | by the issuer:
-- src:43896 | (i) an existing shareholder of the issuer;
-- src:43898 | (ii) an existing holder of a debenture of the issuer;
-- src:43902 | (iia) an existing holder of an SDR with shares or
-- src:43903 | debentures of the issuer as the underlying securities;
-- src:43910 | (iii) where the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:43911 | contracts offered are units or derivatives of units in a
-- src:43912 | business trust, or SDRs with units in a business trust
-- src:43913 | as the underlying securities —
-- src:43915 | (A) an existing unitholder of the business trust;
-- src:43917 | (B) an existing holder of derivatives of units in the
-- src:43918 | business trust; or
-- src:43920 | (C) an existing holder of an SDR with units in the
-- src:43921 | business trust as the underlying securities;
-- src:43925 | (iv) a holder of units of shares or debentures of the issuer;
-- src:43929 | (b) such borrowing is made under an agreement or
-- src:43930 | arrangement between the issuer and the person
-- src:43931 | mentioned in paragraph (a) which promises the issue or
-- src:43932 | allotment of securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:43933 | contracts by the issuer to the person at the same time or
-- src:43934 | shortly after the offer; and
-- src:43940 | (c) in the case of an offer of securities-based derivatives
-- src:43941 | contracts, the obligations under the contracts are not
-- src:43942 | obligations to be discharged by one party to the other at
-- src:43943 | some future time by cash settlement only.
@ref s 273(1A) (src:43887-43943)
GIVEN
    `the securities or contracts being offered are borrowed by the issuer solely for the purpose of facilitating the offer, from an existing shareholder, debenture holder, SDR holder, unitholder, holder of derivatives of units or holder of units of shares or debentures of the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being offered borrowed by the issuer, solely for the purpose of facilitating the offer, from an existing shareholder, an existing holder of a debenture, an existing holder of an SDR, an existing unitholder or holder of derivatives of units of the business trust, or a holder of units of shares or debentures of the issuer?
    `the issuer is treated as having borrowed the securities under section 273(1AAA)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 273(1AAA) the issuer is treated as having borrowed the securities being offered` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the borrowing is made under an agreement or arrangement between the issuer and the lender which promises the issue or allotment of securities or contracts by the issuer to the lender at the same time or shortly after the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the borrowing made under an agreement or arrangement between the issuer and the lender which promises the issue or allotment of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts by the issuer to the lender at the same time or shortly after the offer?
    `the offer is an offer of securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the obligations under the contracts are to be discharged by one party to the other at some future time by cash settlement only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the obligations under the contracts to be discharged by one party to the other at some future time by cash settlement only?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1A) the offer is excluded from paragraphs (d), (da), (e), (ea) and (h) of subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF (`the securities or contracts being offered are borrowed by the issuer solely for the purpose of facilitating the offer, from an existing shareholder, debenture holder, SDR holder, unitholder, holder of derivatives of units or holder of units of shares or debentures of the issuer` OR (`the issuer is treated as having borrowed the securities under section 273(1AAA)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND `the borrowing is made under an agreement or arrangement between the issuer and the lender which promises the issue or allotment of securities or contracts by the issuer to the lender at the same time or shortly after the offer` AND ((NOT `the offer is an offer of securities-based derivatives contracts`) OR (NOT `the obligations under the contracts are to be discharged by one party to the other at some future time by cash settlement only`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts does not come within subsection (1)(d), (da), (e), (ea) or (h) if"
    -- FORK s273-1A | s 273(1A) | `s 273(1A) the offer is excluded from paragraphs (d), (da), (e), (ea) and (h) of subsection (1)` | took JUST FALSE where a limb (a), (b) or (c) is unmet: the exclusion's "if" is not met, which says nothing about whether the offer comes within the paragraph (that is the paragraph's own function) | other reading NOTHING | licence {IN-SHORT} ("if") and {CC}; under "Marginal readings for a lawyer". Limb (c) is read as applying only to an offer of securities-based derivatives contracts ("in the case of").

-- src:43949 | (1AAA) For the purposes of subsection (1A)(a), the issuer is
-- src:43950 | treated as having borrowed the securities being offered for the
-- src:43951 | purpose of facilitating an offer of securities if —
-- src:43953 | (a) where the securities being offered are not SDRs — the
-- src:43954 | issuer borrowed SDRs with those securities as the
-- src:43955 | underlying securities; or
-- src:43957 | (b) where the securities being offered are SDRs — the issuer
-- src:43958 | borrowed securities that are to form the underlying
-- src:43959 | securities of those SDRs.
@ref s 273(1AAA) (src:43949-43959)
GIVEN
    `the securities being offered are SDRs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities being offered SDRs?
    `the issuer borrowed SDRs with the securities being offered as the underlying securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the issuer borrow SDRs with the securities being offered as the underlying securities?
    `the issuer borrowed securities that are to form the underlying securities of the SDRs being offered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the issuer borrow securities that are to form the underlying securities of the SDRs being offered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1AAA) the issuer is treated as having borrowed the securities being offered` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the securities being offered are SDRs`)
    THEN (IF `the issuer borrowed SDRs with the securities being offered as the underlying securities` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the securities being offered are not SDRs — the issuer borrowed SDRs with those securities as the underlying securities"
    ELSE (IF `the issuer borrowed securities that are to form the underlying securities of the SDRs being offered` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the securities being offered are SDRs — the issuer borrowed securities that are to form the underlying securities of those SDRs"

-- src:43966 | (1B) Subdivision (1A) of this Division does not apply to any offer
-- src:43967 | of units in a business trust or derivatives of units in a business trust of
-- src:43968 | a kind described in subsection (1)(b), (c), (cc), (cl) or (j).
@ref s 273(1B) (src:43966-43968)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of units in a business trust or derivatives of units in a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of units in a business trust, or of derivatives of units in a business trust?
    `the offer is of a kind described in paragraph (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 273(1)(b) the offer is made in connection with an acquisition offer for the shares of an unlisted corporation` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the offer is of a kind described in paragraph (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 273(1)(c) the offer is made in connection with a compromise or arrangement of an unlisted corporation` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the offer is of a kind described in paragraph (cc)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 273(1)(cc) the offer is an offer to enter into an underwriting agreement` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the offer is of a kind described in paragraph (cl)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 273(1)(cl) the offer of units or derivatives of units is made to existing holders of an unlisted business trust, or a non-primary listing` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the offer is of a kind described in paragraph (j)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 273(1)(j) the offer of securities by a trustee-manager to a qualifying person` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1B) Subdivision (1A) of this Division does not apply to the offer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offer is an offer of units in a business trust or derivatives of units in a business trust`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any offer of units in a business trust or derivatives of units in a business trust of a kind described in subsection (1)(b), (c), (cc), (cl) or (j)"
        IF (`the offer is of a kind described in paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the offer is of a kind described in paragraph (c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the offer is of a kind described in paragraph (cc)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the offer is of a kind described in paragraph (cl)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the offer is of a kind described in paragraph (j)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of a kind described in subsection (1)(b), (c), (cc), (cl) or (j)"
    -- FORK s273-1B | s 273(1B) | `s 273(1B) Subdivision (1A) of this Division does not apply to the offer` | took NOTHING where the offer is not of a kind described (the flat negative "does not apply" is limited to those kinds, so outside them the text is silent) | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {P-c} (a scope limit with no "only")

§ `s 273(2) and (4): the expenses condition and the qualifying person`

-- src:43972 | (2) An offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:43973 | comes within subsection (1)(i), (ia), (j) or (k) only if no selling or
-- src:43974 | promotional expenses are paid or incurred in connection with the
-- src:43975 | offer other than those incurred —
-- src:43977 | (a) for administrative or professional services; or
-- src:43979 | (b) by way of commission or fee for services rendered by —
-- src:43981 | (i) the holder of a capital markets services licence to
-- src:43982 | deal in capital markets products that are securities or
-- src:43983 | securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:43985 | (ii) an exempt person in respect of dealing in capital
-- src:43986 | markets products that are securities or
-- src:43987 | securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:43989 | (iii) a person who is licensed, approved, authorised or
-- src:43990 | otherwise regulated under the laws, codes or other
-- src:43991 | requirements of any foreign jurisdiction in respect of
-- src:43992 | dealing in capital markets products that are securities
-- src:43993 | or securities‑based derivatives contracts; or
-- src:43995 | (iv) a person who is exempt from the laws, codes or
-- src:43996 | requirements mentioned in sub‑paragraph (iii) in
-- src:43997 | respect of dealing in capital markets products that are
-- src:43998 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts.
@ref s 273(2) (src:43972-43998)
GIVEN
    `the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with the offer` IS A LIST OF `s 272A(1)(d) kind of selling or promotional expense` @desc What are the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with the offer? (An empty list: none are paid or incurred.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(2) no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred other than those the subsection allows` MEANS
    `s 272A(1)(d) the selling or promotional expenses are ones the exemption allows` `the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with the offer`
    -- The kinds of s 273(2)(a), (b)(i) to (iv) are the kinds of s 272A(1)(d): administrative or professional services, and commission or fee for services rendered by the four persons named.

-- src:44006 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (1)(i), (ia), (j) and (k) —
-- src:44008 | (a) a person is a qualifying person in relation to an entity if the
-- src:44009 | person is —
-- src:44011 | (i) a bona fide director or equivalent person, former
-- src:44012 | director or equivalent person, consultant, adviser,
-- src:44013 | employee or former employee of the entity or a
-- src:44018 | related corporation of that entity (being a
-- src:44019 | corporation); or
-- src:44021 | (ii) the spouse, widow, widower or a child, adopted child
-- src:44022 | or stepchild below the age of 18, of such director or
-- src:44023 | equivalent person, former director or equivalent
-- src:44024 | person, employee or former employee; and
@ref s 273(4)(a) (src:44006-44024)
GIVEN
    `the person is a bona fide director or equivalent person, former director or equivalent person, consultant, adviser, employee or former employee of the entity or of a related corporation of the entity (being a corporation)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a bona fide director or equivalent person, former director or equivalent person, consultant, adviser, employee or former employee of the entity, or of a related corporation of the entity (being a corporation)?
    `the person is the spouse, widow, widower or a child, adopted child or stepchild below the age of 18, of such a director, equivalent person, former director, employee or former employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the spouse, widow or widower, or a child, adopted child or stepchild below the age of 18, of such a director or equivalent person, former director or equivalent person, employee or former employee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(4)(a) the person is a qualifying person in relation to the entity` MEANS
    IF `the person is a bona fide director or equivalent person, former director or equivalent person, consultant, adviser, employee or former employee of the entity or of a related corporation of the entity (being a corporation)` OR `the person is the spouse, widow, widower or a child, adopted child or stepchild below the age of 18, of such a director, equivalent person, former director, employee or former employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is a qualifying person in relation to an entity if the person is"

-- src:44026 | (b) a person is a qualifying person in relation to a business trust
-- src:44027 | if the person is —
-- src:44029 | (i) a bona fide director or equivalent person, former
-- src:44030 | director or equivalent person, consultant, adviser,
-- src:44031 | employee or former employee of the trustee‑manager
-- src:44032 | of the business trust or a related corporation of that
-- src:44033 | trustee‑manager (being a corporation); or
-- src:44035 | (ii) the spouse, widow, widower or a child, adopted child
-- src:44036 | or stepchild below the age of 18, of such director or
-- src:44037 | equivalent person, former director or equivalent
-- src:44038 | person, employee or former employee.
@ref s 273(4)(b) (src:44026-44038)
GIVEN
    `the person is a bona fide director or equivalent person, former director or equivalent person, consultant, adviser, employee or former employee of the trustee-manager of the business trust or of a related corporation of the trustee-manager (being a corporation)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a bona fide director or equivalent person, former director or equivalent person, consultant, adviser, employee or former employee of the trustee-manager of the business trust, or of a related corporation of that trustee-manager (being a corporation)?
    `the person is the spouse, widow, widower or a child, adopted child or stepchild below the age of 18, of such a director, equivalent person, former director, employee or former employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the spouse, widow or widower, or a child, adopted child or stepchild below the age of 18, of such a director or equivalent person, former director or equivalent person, employee or former employee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(4)(b) the person is a qualifying person in relation to the business trust` MEANS
    IF `the person is a bona fide director or equivalent person, former director or equivalent person, consultant, adviser, employee or former employee of the trustee-manager of the business trust or of a related corporation of the trustee-manager (being a corporation)` OR `the person is the spouse, widow, widower or a child, adopted child or stepchild below the age of 18, of such a director, equivalent person, former director, employee or former employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is a qualifying person in relation to a business trust if the person is"

§ `s 273(1)(d) to (k): listed securities, derivatives, and qualifying persons`


-- src:43701 | (d) it is an offer of shares or debentures (not being such
-- src:43702 | excluded shares or excluded debentures as the Authority
-- src:43707 | may prescribe) that have been previously issued, are listed
-- src:43708 | for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange, and are
-- src:43709 | traded on the exchange;
@ref s 273(1)(d) (src:43701-43709)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of shares or debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of shares or debentures?
    `the Authority has prescribed the securities as excluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed the securities, units or contracts as excluded for the paragraph (excluded shares, excluded debentures, excluded units in a business trust, or excluded securities-based derivatives contracts, by regulations made under section 341)?
    `the securities have been previously issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the securities, units, SDRs or contracts been previously issued?
    `the securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities, units, SDRs or contracts listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange?
    `the securities are traded on the approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities, units, SDRs or contracts traded on the approved exchange?
    `the offer is excluded by subsection (1A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 273(1A) the offer is excluded from paragraphs (d), (da), (e), (ea) and (h) of subsection (1)` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(d) the offer is an offer of previously issued shares or debentures listed and traded on an approved exchange` MEANS
    IF (`the offer is excluded by subsection (1A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (NOT (`the offer is an offer of shares or debentures` AND (NOT `the Authority has prescribed the securities as excluded`) AND `the securities have been previously issued` AND `the securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange` AND `the securities are traded on the approved exchange`))
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is an offer of shares or debentures (not being such excluded shares or excluded debentures as the Authority may prescribe) that have been previously issued, are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange, and are traded on the exchange"
    ELSE (IF `the offer is excluded by subsection (1A)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE)  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether subsection (1A) excludes the offer is not known

