-- src:43777 | (ii) all underlying securities of the securities‑based
-- src:43778 | derivatives contracts have been previously issued
-- src:43779 | and are listed for quotation on an organised market
-- src:43780 | (not being such excluded organised market as may be
-- src:43781 | prescribed by regulations made under section 341);
-- src:43782 | and
-- src:43784 | (iii) either of the following is satisfied:
-- src:43786 | (A) an application has been or will be made for
-- src:43787 | permission for the securities‑based derivatives
-- src:43788 | contracts to be listed for quotation or quoted on
-- src:43789 | an approved exchange;
-- src:43791 | (B) the offer complies with such disclosure
-- src:43792 | requirements prescribed by regulations made
-- src:43793 | under section 341;
@ref s 273(1)(g) (src:43768-43793)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the Authority has prescribed the securities as excluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed the securities, units or contracts as excluded for the paragraph (excluded shares, excluded debentures, excluded units in a business trust, or excluded securities-based derivatives contracts, by regulations made under section 341)?
    `the obligations under the contracts are to be discharged by one party to the other at some future time by cash settlement only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the obligations under the contracts to be discharged by one party to the other at some future time by cash settlement only?
    `all underlying securities of the contracts have been previously issued and are listed for quotation on an organised market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all underlying securities of the contracts been previously issued, and are they listed for quotation on an organised market?
    `the organised market is an excluded organised market the Authority has prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the organised market an excluded organised market that the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
    `an application has been or will be made for permission for the contracts to be listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made, or will one be made, for permission for the contracts to be listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange?
    `the offer complies with the disclosure requirements the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offer comply with the disclosure requirements the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(g) the offer is an offer of cash-settled securities-based derivatives contracts over securities listed on an organised market` MEANS
    IF `the offer is an offer of securities-based derivatives contracts` AND (NOT `the Authority has prescribed the securities as excluded`) AND `the obligations under the contracts are to be discharged by one party to the other at some future time by cash settlement only` AND `all underlying securities of the contracts have been previously issued and are listed for quotation on an organised market` AND (NOT `the organised market is an excluded organised market the Authority has prescribed`) AND (`an application has been or will be made for permission for the contracts to be listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange` OR `the offer complies with the disclosure requirements the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is an offer of securities‑based derivatives contracts (not being such excluded securities‑based derivatives contracts as may be prescribed by regulations made under section 341) where"

