-- src:43826 | parties;
@ref s 273(1)(i) (src:43819-43826)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of securities (not being SDRs) or securities-based derivatives contracts of an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of securities (not being sponsored depositary receipts, "SDRs") or securities-based derivatives contracts of an entity?
    `the offer is made by an entity to a qualifying person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made by an entity to a person who is a qualifying person in relation to that entity (section 273(4))?
    `the person offered is a qualifying person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 273(4)(a) the person is a qualifying person in relation to the entity` (or, for a business trust, `s 273(4)(b)`) answer for the person offered? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the securities or contracts are to be held by or for the benefit of the qualifying person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or contracts to be held by or for the benefit of the qualifying person?
    `the securities or contracts are those of the entity or of any of its related parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or contracts those of the entity or of any of its related parties?
    `the expenses condition of subsection (2) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 273(2) no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred other than those the subsection allows` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(i) the offer is made by an entity to a qualifying person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the expenses condition of subsection (2) is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT (`the offer is an offer of securities (not being SDRs) or securities-based derivatives contracts of an entity` AND `the offer is made by an entity to a qualifying person` AND `the securities or contracts are to be held by or for the benefit of the qualifying person` AND `the securities or contracts are those of the entity or of any of its related parties`)) OR (`the person offered is a qualifying person` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts comes within subsection (1)(i), (ia), (j) or (k) only if no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred"
        IF (`the expenses condition of subsection (2) is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the person offered is a qualifying person` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the expenses condition or the qualifying person is not answered

-- src:43830 | (ia) it is an offer of SDRs, whether or not previously issued,
-- src:43831 | made or treated under section 239AA as made by an entity
-- src:43832 | to a qualifying person, where the SDRs are to be held by or
-- src:43833 | for the benefit of the qualifying person, and the underlying
-- src:43834 | securities of the SDRs are the securities of that entity or
-- src:43835 | any of its related parties;
@ref s 273(1)(ia) (src:43830-43835)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of SDRs made, or treated under section 239AA as made, by the entity to a qualifying person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of SDRs, whether or not previously issued, made or treated under section 239AA as made by the entity to a qualifying person? (Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (1A), another part's answer.)
    `the person offered is a qualifying person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 273(4)(a) the person is a qualifying person in relation to the entity` (or, for a business trust, `s 273(4)(b)`) answer for the person offered? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the securities or contracts are to be held by or for the benefit of the qualifying person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or contracts to be held by or for the benefit of the qualifying person?
    `the underlying securities of the SDRs are the securities of the entity or any of its related parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the underlying securities of the SDRs the securities of the entity or of any of its related parties?
    `the expenses condition of subsection (2) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 273(2) no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred other than those the subsection allows` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1)(ia) the offer is an offer of SDRs made or treated as made by an entity to a qualifying person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the expenses condition of subsection (2) is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT (`the offer is an offer of SDRs made, or treated under section 239AA as made, by the entity to a qualifying person` AND `the securities or contracts are to be held by or for the benefit of the qualifying person` AND `the underlying securities of the SDRs are the securities of the entity or any of its related parties`)) OR (`the person offered is a qualifying person` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts comes within subsection (1)(i), (ia), (j) or (k) only if no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred"
        IF (`the expenses condition of subsection (2) is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the person offered is a qualifying person` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the expenses condition or the qualifying person is not answered

