        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts comes within subsection (1)(i), (ia), (j) or (k) only if no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred"
        IF (`the expenses condition of subsection (2) is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the person offered is a qualifying person` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the expenses condition or the qualifying person is not answered

