§ `s 273(5) to (8B): the Authority's declaration, conditions, offences and the bar on advertising`

-- src:44044 | (5) Where, on the application of any person interested, the
-- src:44045 | Authority declares that circumstances exist whereby —
-- src:44047 | (a) the cost of providing a prospectus for an offer of securities
-- src:44048 | or securities‑based derivatives contracts outweighs the
-- src:44049 | resulting protection to investors; or
-- src:44051 | (b) it would not be prejudicial to the public interest if a
-- src:44052 | prospectus were dispensed with for an offer of securities or
-- src:44053 | securities‑based derivatives contracts,
-- src:44055 | then Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than
-- src:44056 | section 257) do not apply to such an offer for a period of 6 months
-- src:44057 | from the date of the declaration.
@ref s 273(5) (src:44044-44057)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has made a declaration, on the application of a person interested, that circumstances exist whereby the cost of providing a prospectus outweighs the resulting protection to investors, or a prospectus may be dispensed with without prejudice to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, on the application of a person interested, declared that circumstances exist whereby (a) the cost of providing a prospectus for the offer outweighs the resulting protection to investors, or (b) it would not be prejudicial to the public interest if a prospectus were dispensed with for the offer?
    `the day of the declaration` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the declaration made?
    `the day of the offer` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the offer made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(5) the offer is within the period of 6 months from the date of the Authority's declaration` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Authority has made a declaration, on the application of a person interested, that circumstances exist whereby the cost of providing a prospectus outweighs the resulting protection to investors, or a prospectus may be dispensed with without prejudice to the public interest`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where, on the application of any person interested, the Authority declares that circumstances exist whereby"
        IF (`the day of the offer` AT LEAST `the day of the declaration`) AND (`the day of the offer` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the day of the declaration` 6 Months))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply to such an offer for a period of 6 months from the date of the declaration"
    -- FORK s273-5 | s 273(5) | `s 273(5) the offer is within the period of 6 months from the date of the Authority's declaration` | took the 6 months as beginning with the day of the declaration (keel P10) and JUST FALSE outside the period (a period the text fixes in its own words), NOTHING where no declaration is shown | other reading the offer on the day of the declaration is outside the period | licence {P-a} and {P-c}

-- src:44063 | (6) The Authority may, on making a declaration under
-- src:44064 | subsection (5), impose such conditions or restrictions on the offer
-- src:44065 | as it may determine.
@ref s 273(6) (src:44063-44065)
GIVEN
    `the Authority is making a declaration under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority making a declaration under section 273(5) about the offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(6) the Authority may impose conditions or restrictions on the offer` MEANS
    IF `the Authority is making a declaration under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Authority may, on making a declaration under subsection (5), impose such conditions or restrictions on the offer as it may determine"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
    -- FORK s273-6 | s 273(6) | `s 273(6) the Authority may impose conditions or restrictions on the offer` | took JUST FALSE where the Authority is not making a declaration: "on making" is a gate of the "where", "when", "upon" kind, which the delegated-definitions ruling's item (c) counts as "where", and the periods ruling's item (b) answers JUST FALSE for a failed "where" | other reading NOTHING (a function named for a power whose gate failed, limit 1 of the grant ruling) | licence {DEF-c} and {P-b}; {G3} says to list a "may" function with such a gate and not to change it, and this is the split site (ii) of the brief

-- src:44070 | (7) A declaration made under subsection (5) is final.
@ref s 273(7) (src:44070-44070)
GIVEN
    `a declaration has been made under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a declaration been made under section 273(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(7) the declaration made under subsection (5) is final` MEANS
    IF `a declaration has been made under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a declaration made under subsection (5)

-- src:44072 | (8) Any person who contravenes any of the conditions or
-- src:44073 | restrictions specified in the declaration made under subsection (5)
-- src:44074 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:44075 | not exceeding $50,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- src:44076 | further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:44077 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 273(8) (src:44072-44077)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes a condition or restriction specified in the declaration made under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene any of the conditions or restrictions specified in the declaration made under section 273(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(8) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes a condition or restriction specified in the declaration made under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person who contravenes any of the conditions or restrictions specified in the declaration made under subsection (5) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
    -- FORK s273-8 | s 273(8) | `s 273(8) the person is guilty of an offence` | took JUST FALSE where the contravention element is unmet (this provision's own question) | other reading NOTHING | licence {G2} and the brief's split site (i)

@ref s 273(8) (src:44072-44077)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 273(8) the penalty for the offence` MEANS Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000


-- src:44079 | (8A) A person must not —
-- src:44081 | (a) advertise an offer or intended offer of any securities or
-- src:44082 | securities‑based derivatives contracts mentioned in
-- src:44083 | subsection (1)(d), (da), (e), (ea), (f), (g) or (h); or
-- src:44089 | (b) publish a statement that —
-- src:44091 | (i) directly or indirectly, refers to an offer or intended
-- src:44092 | offer of any securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:44093 | contracts mentioned in subsection (1)(d), (da), (e),
-- src:44094 | (ea), (f), (g) or (h); or
-- src:44100 | (ii) is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe
-- src:44101 | for or purchase the securities or securities‑based
-- src:44102 | derivatives contracts to which the offer relates,
-- src:44104 | unless the advertisement or publication complies with such
-- src:44105 | requirements as may be prescribed by regulations made under
-- src:44106 | section 341.
@ref s 273(8A) (src:44079-44106)
GIVEN
    `the person advertises an offer or intended offer of securities or contracts mentioned in subsection (1)(d), (da), (e), (ea), (f), (g) or (h)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person advertise an offer or intended offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts mentioned in section 273(1)(d), (da), (e), (ea), (f), (g) or (h)?
    `the person publishes a statement that directly or indirectly refers to such an offer or intended offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person publish a statement that, directly or indirectly, refers to an offer or intended offer of securities or contracts mentioned in section 273(1)(d), (da), (e), (ea), (f), (g) or (h)?
    `the person publishes a statement that is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase the securities or contracts to which the offer relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person publish a statement that is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase the securities or contracts to which the offer relates?
    `the advertisement or publication complies with the requirements prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement or publication comply with the requirements the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(8A) the person must not advertise or publish what the subsection bars` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person advertises an offer or intended offer of securities or contracts mentioned in subsection (1)(d), (da), (e), (ea), (f), (g) or (h)` OR `the person publishes a statement that directly or indirectly refers to such an offer or intended offer` OR `the person publishes a statement that is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase the securities or contracts to which the offer relates`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of an advertisement or a statement of the kinds it names
        IF `the advertisement or publication complies with the requirements prescribed by regulations made under section 341`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the advertisement or publication complies with such requirements as may be prescribed by regulations made under section 341"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:44110 | (8B) Any person who contravenes subsection (8A), or who
-- src:44111 | knowingly authorises or permits the publication or dissemination
-- src:44112 | of any advertisement or statement referred to in that subsection, shall
-- src:44113 | be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:44114 | exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:44115 | 12 months or to both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- src:44116 | further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:44117 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 273(8B) (src:44110-44117)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes subsection (8A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene section 273(8A)?
    `the person knowingly authorises or permits the publication or dissemination of an advertisement or statement referred to in subsection (8A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person knowingly authorise or permit the publication or dissemination of an advertisement or statement referred to in section 273(8A)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(8B) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes subsection (8A)` OR `the person knowingly authorises or permits the publication or dissemination of an advertisement or statement referred to in subsection (8A)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person who contravenes subsection (8A), or who knowingly authorises or permits the publication or dissemination of any advertisement or statement referred to in that subsection, shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
    -- FORK s273-8B | s 273(8B) | `s 273(8B) the person is guilty of an offence` | took JUST FALSE where neither element is shown (this provision's own question) | other reading NOTHING | licence {G2} and the brief's split site (i)

@ref s 273(8B) (src:44110-44117)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 273(8B) the penalty for the offence` MEANS Penalty OF 50000, 12, TRUE, 5000

§ `s 273: the duty of subsection (8A) as a regulative rule`

DECLARE `s 273 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 273 a person`

DECLARE `s 273 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 273(8A) advertise or publish what the subsection bars`

-- src:44079 | (8A) A person must not —
-- src:44081 | (a) advertise an offer or intended offer of any securities or
@ref s 273(8A) (src:44079-44081)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 273 party` `s 273 act`
`s 273(8A) the bar on advertising or publishing` MEANS
    PARTY `s 273 a person`
    SHANT `s 273(8A) advertise or publish what the subsection bars`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 273 a person` BECAUSE "the person advertised or published what section 273(8A) bars, without complying with the requirements prescribed under section 341"

§ `s 273(1): the offer is exempt if it comes within any paragraph`

DECLARE `s 273(1) a paragraph and its answer` HAS
    `the paragraph` IS A STRING
    `the answer of the paragraph` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the paragraphs and their answers` IS A LIST OF `s 273(1) a paragraph and its answer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 273(1) the number of paragraphs that hold` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the paragraphs and their answers`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF (p's `the answer of the paragraph`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN 1 PLUS (`s 273(1) the number of paragraphs that hold` rest)
        ELSE `s 273(1) the number of paragraphs that hold` rest

GIVEN `the paragraphs and their answers` IS A LIST OF `s 273(1) a paragraph and its answer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 273(1) the number of paragraphs that are not answered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the paragraphs and their answers`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF (p's `the answer of the paragraph`) EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN 1 PLUS (`s 273(1) the number of paragraphs that are not answered` rest)
        ELSE `s 273(1) the number of paragraphs that are not answered` rest

-- src:43384 | 273.—(1) Subject to subsection (5), Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this
-- src:43385 | Division (other than section 257) do not apply to an offer of securities
-- src:43386 | or securities‑based derivatives contracts if —
@ref s 273(1) (src:43384-43386)
GIVEN
    `the paragraphs and their answers` IS A LIST OF `s 273(1) a paragraph and its answer`  @desc For each of paragraphs (a) to (k) of section 273(1) that could apply: the paragraph's label and what its function answers. Pass NOTHING as the answer where you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273(1) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 273(1) the number of paragraphs that hold` `the paragraphs and their answers` AT LEAST 1
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 273(1) the number of paragraphs that are not answered` `the paragraphs and their answers` AT LEAST 1
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a paragraph is not answered, and no answered paragraph holds
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply to an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts if"
    -- FORK s273-1 | s 273(1) | `s 273(1) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` | took JUST FALSE where every paragraph the caller lists is answered and none holds (the "if" list is the text's only route, apart from the Authority's declaration in subsection (5), which has its own function) | other reading NOTHING ("if A then B" does not say "if not A then not B"); and an empty list answers JUST FALSE, as no paragraph holds | licence {IN-SHORT}; under "Marginal readings for a lawyer". "Subject to subsection (5)" is read as the Authority's declaration being another route, not a limit on this one.
